samba-adws (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian packaging (samba-adws#6). Installs the service as a payload
    under /usr/share/samba-adws with a systemd unit, the samba-adws command
    MODULE.yaml has declared since it was written, and the configuration
    under /etc/hardensamba/samba-adws/ as a conffile. Replaces the
    from-checkout installer as the documented path; that script remains for
    a source install.
  * Leave the unit disabled on every controller (contract 4.2). The
    conditional enable never took effect: debhelper's own snippet records
    the unit's state first and the helper defers to it (samba-adws#45).
  * Make the checkout installer put the package's files at the package's
    paths, printed for CI to diff against dpkg -L; its own unit template is
    gone, the package's unit is the one unit.
  * Add CI: the level-0 suite, flake8 and mypy on debian:stable, and the
    package built, checked with lintian, installed and compared with the
    installer.

 -- HardenSamba <hardensamba@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
